WHAT WAS RENDERED BESIDE THE PROBE, 23 September 2026.

The container's egress to the Supabase host is denied by organisation policy,
so `/price/area/[id]` cannot be rendered against the live project from here.
It was rendered instead against a local PostgREST-shaped reader holding ONE
share row with the shape and the string-encoded bigints PostgREST actually
sends, which is what the page reads through `shareById`:

  GET /price/area/00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000cafe            200
    <title>3 bedroom flats in Lekki Phase 1 | Vallo</title>
    og:title        3 bedroom flats in Lekki Phase 1
    og:description  Asking N7.5m to N9m a year. Based on 9 Vallo listings, September 2026
    og:image        .../opengraph-image-...  image/png  1200x630
    card            "3 bedroom flats in Lekki Phase 1" / range / "Based on 9
                    Vallo listings, September 2026" / "Asking prices, not sold
                    prices. vallo.ng" / "This is not a valuation." in full

  GET /price/area/<an id with no row>                             200
    the "This card is not here" state, one sentence for all three causes

  GET .../opengraph-image                     200 image/png 1200x630, 61 KB
  GET .../opengraph-image (no row)            200 image/png 1200x630, the mark
                                              and NO FIGURES

  GET /preview/price/share                    200, both states on one page

THE FIRST IMAGE PRINTED THE MONEY AS A TOFU BOX and that is recorded because
it is the class of fault that ships. Satori has no system font fallback and
`@vercel/og` fetches one per missing glyph at render time; that request
answered 400 for the naira sign, and Geist, the font it bundles, does not
carry U+20A6 either (726 codepoints, the euro among them, not this one). The
route now reads unsubsetted Inter from beside itself, so the picture of
somebody's money has no network dependency in the middle of it.
